    "name": "Portable Flashing Package: Engineering Firmware for Innioasis Y2 (Android 4.4 AOSP base - MT6582))",
    "body": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://innioasis.app/guide.html?repo=y1-community%2Fy2-ata-rom&amp;tag=y2-ata#download-updater\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/main/.mirror-assets/release-button-updater.svg\" width=\"400\" alt=\"Get it on Updater CE - with guided install\"></a>\n</p>\n\n### Downloads\n\n**Y2 \u00b7 Stock**\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/releases/download/y2-ata/rom_y2-windows.zip\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/main/.mirror-assets/release-button-windows.svg\" width=\"400\" alt=\"Download .zip for Windows for Y2 \u00b7 Stock - x86-64 \u00b7 portable package\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/releases/download/y2-ata/rom_y2-linux.zip\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/main/.mirror-assets/release-button-linux.svg\" width=\"400\" alt=\"Download .zip for Linux for Y2 \u00b7 Stock - x86-64 \u00b7 portable package\"></a>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/releases/download/y2-ata/rom_y2-linux-arm64.zip\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/main/.mirror-assets/release-button-linux-arm64.svg\" width=\"400\" alt=\"Download .zip for Linux arm64 for Y2 \u00b7 Stock - portable package\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/releases/download/y2-ata/rom_y2-macos.zip\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y1-community/y2-ata-rom-mirror/main/.mirror-assets/release-button-macos.svg\" width=\"400\" alt=\"Download .zip for macOS 12+ for Y2 \u00b7 Stock - Intel + Apple silicon\"></a>\n</p>\n\n---\n\n# This is a bare android firmware for modifications to the Innioasis Y2 - it includes flash_tool.exe to install it from Windows systems\r\n# This is not suitable for everyday use - the original firmware 